WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.936
Optional provisions may be included at the insurer’s choice.

00:00:02.936 --> 00:00:06.524
Under change of occupation, if Rosa moves from office estimating to

00:00:06.524 --> 00:00:10.113
climbing poles, a more hazardous job, benefits are reduced to what

00:00:10.113 --> 00:00:13.375
her premium would have bought at the new occupation’s rate.

00:00:13.375 --> 00:00:16.637
If she moves to a less hazardous job, premium drops

00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:19.899
and the excess is refunded from the date of change.

00:00:19.899 --> 00:00:24.140
Under misstatement of age, if she gave the wrong birth date, benefits are

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.054
adjusted to what the premium would have purchased at her true age.

00:00:28.054 --> 00:00:30.990
Neither provision voids the policy; both correct the bargain.

00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:35.466
Other insurance in this company limits the total coverage one

00:00:35.466 --> 00:00:39.943
insurer will carry on a person; excess premium is refunded.

00:00:39.943 --> 00:00:45.762
Insurance with other companies addresses duplicate coverage the insurer was not told about.

00:00:45.762 --> 00:00:49.791
On expense-incurred benefits, the insurer pays only its proportionate

00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:53.820
share of the loss and refunds the excess premium.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.296
On other benefits, such as disability income, benefits are prorated.

00:00:58.296 --> 00:01:04.564
Relation of earnings to insurance prevents profit from disability: if total disability benefits exceed

00:01:04.564 --> 00:01:10.831
the insured’s earnings at the start of disability, or average earnings over the prior

00:01:10.831 --> 00:01:16.650
two years, benefits are reduced to earnings, never below 200 dollars a month.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:21.765
Unpaid premium lets the insurer deduct any premium due from a claim payment.

00:01:21.765 --> 00:01:26.094
Cancellation by the company permits the insurer to cancel with written

00:01:26.094 --> 00:01:30.422
notice, commonly 45 days under state rules, refunding unearned premium pro

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:34.751
rata; cancellation does not affect a claim that began before it.

00:01:34.751 --> 00:01:40.260
Conformity with state statutes amends any provision that conflicts with the law of the

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:45.769
state where the insured lives so that it meets the minimum the law requires.

00:01:45.769 --> 00:01:50.884
Illegal occupation and intoxicants and narcotics relieve the insurer of liability for losses

00:01:50.884 --> 00:01:56.000
from a felony or illegal occupation, or while intoxicated or under unprescribed narcotics.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:58.625
Three general provisions frame every policy.

00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:04.749
The right to examine, or free look, lets the insured return the policy within

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:10.873
a stated period after delivery, typically ten days for individual health policies and thirty

00:02:10.873 --> 00:02:16.997
days for Medicare supplement and long-term care policies in Maryland, for a full refund.

00:02:16.997 --> 00:02:20.934
The insuring clause is the insurer’s core promise: who

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:24.434
is covered, against which perils, for what benefits.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:27.934
The consideration clause states what the insured gives:

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:31.433
the premium and the statements in the application.

00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:37.120
Together they define the exchange, and the rest of the policy qualifies it.

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.302
Renewability tells you who controls the policy’s future.

00:02:40.302 --> 00:02:44.280
Noncancelable is the strongest: the insurer may neither cancel nor

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:47.860
raise the premium until a stated age, often 65.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:51.837
Guaranteed renewable: the insurer may not cancel or refuse renewal,

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:55.815
but may raise premiums for an entire class of insureds.

00:02:55.815 --> 00:03:00.986
Conditionally renewable: the insurer may refuse renewal only for reasons stated in the

00:03:00.986 --> 00:03:06.157
policy, such as reaching an age or leaving a job, never for health.

00:03:06.157 --> 00:03:09.737
Renewable at the option of the insurer: the insurer

00:03:09.737 --> 00:03:12.919
may refuse renewal at any premium due date.

00:03:12.919 --> 00:03:18.090
Cancelable or nonrenewable term: the insurer may cancel at any time with notice.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:20.362
Two smaller provisions finish the set.

00:03:20.362 --> 00:03:24.906
Interest on claim proceeds requires the insurer to pay interest when a

00:03:24.906 --> 00:03:29.449
claim is paid late; Maryland’s prompt payment law sets the rate, starting

00:03:29.449 --> 00:03:33.993
at 1.5 percent a month on clean claims unpaid after thirty days.

00:03:33.993 --> 00:03:38.537
The military suspension provision lets an insured called to active duty suspend

00:03:38.537 --> 00:03:43.080
the policy, with premium refunded for the suspension period, and reinstate it

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:46.867
without evidence of insurability within a set time after discharge.

00:03:46.867 --> 00:03:52.168
Rosa should know that a noncancelable policy she buys today protects both her coverage

00:03:52.168 --> 00:03:57.090
and her price, while a guaranteed renewable medical plan protects only the coverage.
